{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites","id":1548935,"title":"Running the Free States - 5 - Setites","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-03-03T21:30:56-08:00","id":1548935,"title":"Running the Free States - 5 - Setites","content":"A big part of the backstory of LABN involves the Setites, and the lone Setite NPC is portrayed as an antagonist. However, the Setites are quite underdeveloped as a setting element. So we\u2019ll discuss them here. First though, a brief history of canon.<br /> <br /> The Setite Dawn Cavanaugh arrived in Malibu in 1923 and established her first temple there in the Malibu Hills. She was very successful in attracting adherents and helped make Hollywood a sin city. We\u2019re told that in the days of Don Sebastian Malibu was a major Toreador hangout and a hundred Kindred could gather there spontaneously for a night\u2019s evening. (It\u2019s likely at one of these parties was where the Blount sisters\u2019 father/sire was embraced in 1923.)<br /> <br /> Then in 1944 the Garou of the Black Furies tribe that controlled a caern in Topanga Canyon wiped out the Temple of Set in Malibu as it had corrupted a number of Garou and Kindred. The Garou wiped out many elders who dwelled or visited there. The exact date of this was December 21, 1944 which was the winter solstice. Other than that being the longest night of the year, I\u2019m not sure if that has any special significance. Although if we go by Werewolf: the Apocalypse, there is the winter solstice seasonal Rite of the Winter Winds which ends in a Revel where the Garou remove anything that threatens the caern. So there might be a religious significance to the timing of the Garou attack on the temple. It may have been serendipity that the Lupine assault coincided with the anarch attack (as well as the slaughter of Don Sebastian and other elders at his ranch by what I assume was Christopher Houghton) all on the same night.<br /> <br /> Dawn was not at the temple at this time, but in San Francisco on business. Her biography states she may have been tipped off. If so, it was likely one of the corrupted Garou who warned her. However, it is possible she may have blamed MacNeil\u2019s anarchs as they were heading there until warned off by a female Garou that they had already done so and that Malibu was now free of vampires. She might now have known who actually did it. Dawn stayed in San Francisco for the next two decades, but moved back to Los Angeles after the failed Sabbat invasion. She established a second temple in 1969, this time in the Hollywood Hills.<br /> <br /> This second temple was betrayed by her acolyte Nicholas (likely sometime in the seventies) who wanted to remove her so he could take over. However, his plan failed when he local anarchs to whom he revealed the location of the temple, notified MacNeil and he lead an attack on the second temple that wiped it out. Nicholas likely hoped a small group of neonate anarchs would attack and die in the attempt, but it would provide him an opportunity to slay Dawn himself. Instead, Dawn was once again absent, this time being forewarned by someone in MacNeil\u2019s coterie.<br /> <br /> Dawn fled to Chicago and left that city after the events of Under a Blood Red Moon to gain revenge on MacNeil and then establish a third temple (in that order). Her preferred method is to seduce and corrupt vampires, presumably because they can corrupt others more easily.<br /> <br /> =<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council\">Part 1 - the Anarch Council</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine\">Part 2 - Germaine</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance\">Part 3 - Governance</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs\">Part 4 - Canon Characters &amp; Gangs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549587-running-the-free-states-6-petrodon-and-the-camarilla\">Part 6 - the Camarilla</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club\">Part 7 - San Francisco</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat\">Part 8 - Sabbat</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements\">Part 9 - Crossovers</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552818-running-the-free-states-10-the-oddball-stuff\">Part 10 - Oddballs</a>\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 02-02-2026, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-04T06:59:29-08:00","id":1548947,"title":"","content":"Before I get into any serious discussion of the topic, I took one look at \u2018Malibu Hills\u2019 and vampire surf-and-turf, then thought \u201cBAYWATCH David Hasselhoff Vs Just Another Snake Cult - who wins?\u201d*<br /> <br /> Truly, I have watched far too much BAYWATCH in the last year or two.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>*Answer: The Audience</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, back to the actual topic:-<br /> <br /> (1) It\u2019s interesting to note that while Dawn Cavanaugh hasn\u2019t done very well in the Free States, she has a long record of prospering - or at least operating for long periods - in Camarilla cities.<br /> <br /> I wonder if her training and experience as a Victorian embrace specifically-trained to infiltrate &amp; subvert European colonial society makes it much harder for her to operate outside polite society? (The Anarchs may occasionally be civil, but I doubt the Free States qualify as polite society by any definition).<br /> <br /> <br /> (2) Interestingly, Dawn Canaugh is of the same generation as Hesha Ruhadze (8th) and Abu Ruhadze, the latter\u2019s Sire, is noted as a Setite who \u201c\u2026 also worshipped the Islamic faith\u201d (Possibly suggesting a syncretic approach, merging Setite principles with Islamic theology or vice versa, possibly only suggesting an unusually strong cover as a Muslim holy man - albeit a presumably Unorthodox one).<br /> <br /> Given that Hesha Ruhadze was embraced in the late 17th century and his Sire was still doing the rounds in the late Victorian Age (Dawn Cavanaugh was embraced in AD 1898, Abu Ruhadze is noted to have adopted his newer name in Modern Nights), so I\u2019m tempted to suggest pencilling in Abu Ruhadze as the Sire of Dawn Cavanaugh.<br /> <br /> This is, admittedly, because I\u2019m not sure how to chase down a list of Followers of Set from the Seventh Generation, but it does make sense that a Follower of Set with a strong Islamic connection and a potent Cult of Personality would be able to persuade a Sheikh who participated in the Fall of Khartoum and survived the downfall of the Mahdist Movement to part with one of the women from his following.<br /> <br /> <br /> (3) Incidentally, Cavanaugh\u2019s background as the daughter of a British officer captured in the Fall of Khartoum (family killed in the sack) and given over into the household of a Sheikh is vaguely-possible, but given that she was born in AD 1882 and Khartoum fell early in 1885, there\u2019s absolutely no way she remembers any of it personally.<br /> <br /> It also bears considering that this is exactly the sort of backstory a young woman plucked from North African obscurity by a Setite because of her red hair and then sent to infiltrate European colonial society all across the Middle East (In the interests of subverting it) would conjure up as part of her legend - a legend that might prove equally appealing in 1920s Los Angeles, given the immense popularity of (Amongst others) Mr Rudolph Valentino as THE SHEIKH.<br /> <br /> That it\u2019s a backstory calculated to appeal to Victorian tastes to a degree that makes it hard for a more modern age to swallow might offer an interesting angle on the character - as someone from a very different time and place who has increasing difficulty accommodating herself to modern society (\u201cHence Camarilla city = no probs\u201d as a wag might put it). <br /> <br /> <br /> In any case it seems reasonable to sum up the experience of her confirmable early life as a teenage girl from the household of a North African sheikh, possibly from the Sudan, who was picked out by an Elder Setite (Seventh Generation, remember) because Red hair is strongly associated with Set and presumably because she was (or at least looked) white enough to pass muster in European circles.<br /> <br /> Whether she was actually the daughter of a British officer or had been anywhere near Khartoum in her life is an question whose answer remains lost to Dawn Kavanaugh (Who would most definitely have adopted that name only after becoming a vampire: if she had a Muslim name, it seems to have been dropped a long time ago).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (4) An equally interesting question is how much of a connection Dawn Kavanaugh kept up with her Sire and the Old World Followers of Set - my guess is that, having gone from a mere handmaiden (possibly a slave) in the tents of a back country sheikh into European colonial circles (I.E. The upper crust and higher leadership in political, financial and to a degree social circles) across the Middle East (and as the daughter of a British officer \u2018martyred\u2019 alongside the celebrated Gordon at Khartoum), she might well have gotten used to a degree of comfort almost impossible to maintain as an active subversive in the days of the Great War - hence her move to the Western Hemisphere, which might well have dovetailed neatly with Setite interests in destabilising the Great Power least affected by the First World War.<br /> <br /> This would suggest that Cavanaugh would maintain a generally-positive, albeit distant connection with her Setite elders: on the other hand, the very fact she sailed off to the other side of the world might suggest the desire for that connection to be distant and respectful on her part (and it\u2019s not impossible that her repeated failures in LA - especially the debacle precipitating the fall of the second Temple - might have persuaded the Followers of Set to cut Dawn Cavanaugh loose).<br /> <br /> So the question of how closer her ties to the Setite elders might be remains an open one - though I lean towards the notion that Dawn prefers to avoid close attention from her superiors, at least at this point in her career (It now occurs to me that Nicholas\u2019 bold move against the boss might have been prompted by the suspicion that their elders would be more interested in a success than in questioning exactly which hands they received it from).<br /> <br /> <br /> (5) It seems highly likely that the longest night of the year would be the perfect occasion for a massive party of vampires to \u2026 well, to do anything, really \u2026 and given that the mass gatherings in Malibu had tended to be supremely indulgent, it\u2019s not hard to imagine both the Anarchs and the Garou taking advantage of such a distraction, the Anarchs striking in the core of LA while significant elements of the Toreador leadership were busy elsewhere and the Black Furies popping the local ticks whilst they were rather the worse for their indulgences.<br /> <br /> That this would - at least for the Garou - neatly coincide with one of their many annual rituals involving a killing spree would, of course, be either a very happy coincidence or a further blessing (depending on how one looked at it).<br /> <br /> <br /> (6) It\u2019s interesting to wonder if it might have been one of the corrupted Garou or Kinfolk who have the Black Furies their actionable intelligence - I\u2019d bet on it being a Kinfolk spilled the beans to Dawn Cavanaugh though, if anyone actually did (Given that a Garou getting in touch with one of the Kindred at a time when the local pack is planning an offensive would be very, very noticeable - and extremely dangerous, when the Garou in question are Black Furies rather than Shadow Lords).<br /> <br /> For my money making Dawn Cavanaugh aware of only one, rather than both, of these impending offensives makes more sense on a character level - keeping a safe distance whilst the local Authorities and the local rebels work out who gets to run things, then coming back to help rearrange things once the argument is resolved (Hands free of blood to boot) is a decent plan, but making your way to San Francisco when your temple and your followers are about to be wrecked by Mother Nature\u2019s Hairiest War Machines in Malibu smacks of failure, rather than sound policy.<br /> <br /> Put another way: If Dawn Cavanaugh laid on a Vampire Beach Party at the Temple of Set in order to arrange for her assets to be covered while she kept a safe distance from the brewing strife in LA (All the better to present herself as an innocent - or at least a neutral party - in the aftermath), only to be blindsided by aforesaid Werewolf War Party, then this presents a fairly convincing picture of the Fog of War turning a reasonably shrewd \u2018hand\u2019s off\u2019 policy into a disaster.<br /> <br /> Especially if Dawn being \u2018warned in advance\u2019 was part of a deception plan calculated to remove the Kay clear-thinking vampire at any Setite festivity (aka the Head Priestess) from the equation, all the better to wreck the Temple and it\u2019s congregation.<br /> <br /> <br /> That notion rambled on a little, but I do like the idea that whilst Dawn Cavanaugh\u2019s absence was planned, the plan was based on incompetence intelligence (and possibly on a deception plan, though whether of Garou or Kindred construction I\u2019m not sure).<br /> <br /> <br /> (7) While one enjoys the fact that the ever-subtle Setites were absolutely wrecked by the frequently fangs out, fur on fire Black Furies (\u2018Amazons Vs Snake Cult\u2019 is purest PULP, even when you remove the \u2019werewolf\u2019 and \u2018vampire\u2019 from the equation), some small part of me would have loved to see a shout-out to Vic Stryker and his Eagle\u2019s Nest pack (Burning out Setites is absolutely one of their party tricks and the gang deserve a Last Hurrah before oncoming tragedy hits them like the end of a Golden Age).<br /> <br /> Not least since there\u2019s nothing like brutally wrecking a Follower of Set\u2019a entire world to put a spring in a Silent Strider\u2019s step (and very little more calculated to bring out their Best efforts).<br /> <br /> <br /> (8) Interestingly, the date given for Dawn\u2019s return to LA is AD 1965, so it would seem that the establishment of the second Temple was the fruit of several year\u2019s hard work in the wake of the Sabbat Attack.<br /> <br /> I wonder if any Setites built their bone fides with the Anarchs by playing some role in the fighting? (Or at least in the mopping-up).<br /> <br /> <br /> (9) There doesn\u2019t seem to be very much on Nicholas anywhere, but the mental image of his being very much an LA local to Dawn Cavanaugh\u2019s \u2018blow in\u2019 has been consistent part of my mental image for the character from my first conception of him - your description of the circumstances surrounding the fall of the first Temple make me wonder if he was one of the rare survivors of the attack (and also whether he might have been behind claims - true or false - that the High Priestesses\u2019 absence in San Francisco indicates that she knew the attack was coming, then abandoned her followers &amp; rivals to perish*).<br /> <br /> Incidentally, it\u2019s taken me this long to get a strong mental image for this character, but the mental image of him as a very Sam Spade Private Eye (I.E. a profoundly mercenary chiseler with the face of \u201c\u2026a friendly Satan\u201d) as played by Mr Willem Dafoe has struck me and refuses to be shifted.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m assuming that a Setite would embrace a mercenary PI as a source of intelligence and a means of disseminating disinformation (Or at least arranging some serious blackmail), as well as acquiring somebody who not only knows where the bodies are buried, but knows how to exhume them for fun and profit (Also that \u2018Satanic PI\u2019 would make an excellent, rather subversive villain for Film Noir).<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, should Nicholas need a surname, I\u2019m assuming that it should echo some neighbourhood or district of Los Angeles (To emphasise his nature as a local boy who would have been a local hero, if only he weren\u2019t such a heel - or perhaps as a subtle way to hint at an alias \u2026 or both).<br /> <br /> Nicholas Baldwin? Nicholas Hancock? Nicholas Hyde?<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>*The possibility that she knew the attack was coming, but moved to save herself alone, might be equally damaging (Though a great deal depends on exactly when and in what form the warning arrived).<br /> </i><br /> <br /> (10) Incidentally, the second Temple being located in the Hollywood Hills circa the late 1960s gives me a strong \u2018Manson Family\u2019 vibe - I wonder if making the Brujah convert who may have sold out Nicholas to Jeremy MacNeil (and warned Dawn Cavanaugh to be elsewhere) a Manson Family type would make sense?<br /> <br /> An alternative that occurred to me was an African-American trying to get away from White civilisation and back to Mother Africa could well have fallen in with the impeccably-Egyptian Followers of Set (Having been embraced by Clan Brujah as more of a Black Panther type).<br /> <br /> Actually, making him an more authentic Nation of Islam-type than \u2018Papa Crypt\u2019 might well explain how Dawn got her hooks into him (She having been raised Muslim, albeit apparently low on the social pyramid) - as well as explaining her \u2018In\u2019 to modern LA circa the early 1990s (Back in the days when the Islamic world was mostly the stuff of Arabian Nights to the wider USA, prior to 9/11) in a way that sets up possible plot hooks (One assumes that \u2018Papa Crypt\u2019 would take an interest in somebody hitting at least a few of the same notes as his own preaching and would, above all others, be able to pick out somebody who talks Allah, but may be thinking of a very different god).<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, that should do by now - hopefully none of my notions are overdone!\ud83d\ude42<br /> <br /> Before I go, might one ask if Dawn Cavanaugh\u2019s Nature &amp; Demeanour are listed in any of your sources? I can\u2019t find them online and would appreciate the useful insight into a characterisation that they offer,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-04T07:00:30-08:00","id":1548948,"title":"","content":"P.S. My apologies for any typos - putting this sort of thing together on a smartphone screen can be a tearing nuisance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-04T23:15:59-08:00","id":1548976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites?p=1548947#post1548947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s interesting to wonder if it might have been one of the corrupted Garou or Kinfolk who have the Black Furies their actionable intelligence - I\u2019d bet on it being a Kinfolk spilled the beans to Dawn Cavanaugh though, if anyone actually did</div> </div> </div> </div>That's reasonable. It would certainly be easier for a Setite to corrupt a kinfolk (perhaps unknowingly) than an actual Garou unless we're given individual reasons why a Garou would be that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites?p=1548947#post1548947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestingly, the date given for Dawn\u2019s return to LA is AD 1965, so it would seem that the establishment of the second Temple was the fruit of several year\u2019s hard work in the wake of the Sabbat Attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not clear that she did come back in 1965. LABN states at least twice that the second temple was built in 1969. It's just her biography makes mention that the failed Sabbat invasion in 1965 is what convinced her to come back. She could have come back anytime between 1965-1969 although I would assume it would take some time between her arrival and establishing a new temple. Although we should keep in mind that a temple is simply her haven and where she'd conduct her sacred rites.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites?p=1548947#post1548947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before I go, might one ask if Dawn Cavanaugh\u2019s Nature &amp; Demeanour are listed in any of your sources? I can\u2019t find them online and would appreciate the useful insight into a characterisation that they offer,</div> </div> </div> </div>LABN gives her Nature as Conniver and Demeanor as Deviant.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-04T23:21:10-08:00","id":1548977,"title":"","content":"Dawn should be a formidable opponent, but is nothing really special mechanics wise. She\u2019s not even an ancillae in LABN, being just under a hundred years as a vampire. Her character sheet is fine, but nothing special. The one advantage she has is that her heart is located in an urn at the Grand Temple in Uganda (so she can't be destroyed by anyone in LA). Since Dawn does not have Serpentis 5 (she only has it up to rank 4), we can assume her sire removed her heart and this would compel her to be very loyal to the clan elders (since they can destroy her). It has to be her cunning that makes her dangerous.<br /> <br /> The other reference to Setites in LABN is in the biography of Sir Ralph Hamilton where it says he had some contacts with Setites in the past (he has Serpentis 3), and would be in deep trouble if exposed. We\u2019re not told what this big scandal is, but presumably he was involved enough to be taught the signature Discipline. Since Sir Ralph is from London, I\u2019ll connect him to the Setites in London By Night which is set in the Victorian era. The one Setite depicted, Halim Bey, was embraced fifty years after Sir Ralph, so I\u2019ll use Halim\u2019s sire Sirian instead as the Setite who initially groomed Sir Ralph. Or perhaps go back to the original Setite clanbook and use Sir Marriot D'Urban.<br /> <br /> By herself, Dawn seems unlikely to be a major threat. There is only so much an ST can do with a plan of her seducing someone close to MacNeil so he\u2019ll betray and help destroy him, and then she starts a third temple. It\u2019s likely LABN\u2019s author intended STs to have Dawn blackmail Sir Ralph Hamilton, but I don\u2019t think that it would make that much of a difference. Even adding a mole among MacNeil\u2019s coterie doesn\u2019t give her that much of an edge.<br /> <br /> So we\u2019ll need to be creative in order to make her a real threat. I\u2019ll probably make her at least the short term main antagonist for my chronicle, and have the PCs slowly uncover the menace. But I'll need to boost her up a bit.<br /> <br /> What do the Los Angeles Kindred know of Dawn? I doubt very much she uses her mortal name. It would make sense to use different aliases when she was priestess of the two temples. But do they even have a description of her? She wasn\u2019t around when either temple was destroyed, and it isn\u2019t clear that anyone even knew there was a first setite temple since it was the Lupines who destroyed it.<br /> <br /> I ask because it\u2019s important as to how Dawn will proceed. The safest option is that nobody has a name or description of the previous Setite temple leader. Even a generic description like hot mid-teen jailbait would expose her. Any PC hearing such a description will quickly guess who she is because PCs know they are in a story and always looking for Chekhov\u2019s Gun.<br /> <br /> Having said that, I must note that Dawn is not the only Setite in LA. LABN states that the Setites already have one temple in Beverly Hills and a second in the Encino hills overlooking the San Fernando Valley. Dawn's return simply hints at a third temple. The temple don't necessarily need to help each other, as it's known that rival temples are frequently at odds. But in terms of building the Setites as a faction in the Free States, it's important to note that. The failure of LABN to provide more information on the clan in this regards is just one of its many weaknesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 03-05-2025, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-05T13:39:07-08:00","id":1548991,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, thank you for giving me Dawn Cavanaugh\u2019s Nature &amp; Demeanour (It occurs to me that a key reason for her failure to establish a lasting presence in LA may well be her tendency to destructive, rather than constructive, intrigue - conspiracy being a poor substitute for leadership, particularly when one conspires against rivals within your own organisation).<br /> <br /> Regarding your second post:-<br /> <br /> (1) It\u2019s interesting to wonder if Dawn Cavanaugh is made more or less brave by the fact that her missing heart makes it very nearly impossible to kill her permanently - after all, when you can\u2019t stay dead you can suffer so much more.<br /> <br /> <br /> (2) If I remember correctly, Sir Ralph is one of the Brujah idealists - which might qualify him for the role of the mole who warned Dawn Cavanaugh away from the destruction of the second Temple, though for my money he might work better as a false lead in the Mole Hunt, given he doesn\u2019t seem especially close to MacNeil (Though as a Brujah with some Setite connections, he might be exactly the right Sire for our Mole).<br /> <br /> <br /> (3) I wonder if, at this point in her career, Dawn Cavanaugh works better as someone who gets the plot moving in a way that starts to unravel the Setite designs in LA - it would be a logical progression (or decline) from someone who goes from the founder of Setite fortunes in Los Angeles to more of a liability, through a wealth of infighting and more than one forced retreat.<br /> <br /> Especially given that her core ambition is the foundation of a \u2018Third Temple\u2019 in LA when there are Setite temples already in existence in that territory (Strongly suggesting that either she is not aware of their existence or, more likely, she is not in control of these outposts and not likely to assert any control over them in the near future).<br /> <br /> <br /> (4) As noted above, there\u2019s at least some grounds to believe that \u2018Dawn Cavanaugh\u2019 may be an adopted alias - and I\u2019d bet money she tends to think of herself by an Islamic name, when she thinks of her mortal identity.<br /> <br /> It might also make sense to muddy the waters by showing a certain amount of confusion over whether the Temple of Set\u2019s leader was male or female (Vague memories of Nicholas and Dawn struggling for primacy becoming a historical controversy).<br /> <br /> It does seem reasonable to make the only fixed constant in the vague recollections and friend-of-a-friend accounts that flaming red hair (Our Heroes need a few useful hints to go on, after all).<br /> <br /> Incidentally all honesty, being so discrete as to leave not even a distinct recollection of her strongly suggests that a failure to stand up and be counted was a viable survival strategy, but a key precondition of Dawn Cavanaugh\u2019s failure to establish an enduring Setite presence and maintain unchallenged leadership over her own brood (Presumably a comfortable majority of the Clan in the Free States).<br /> <br /> <br /> (5) I think it would be quite important to establish who leads the Beverly Hills and Encino temples, because it seems highly likely that it is they and not Dawn Cavanaugh who have shaped the fortunes of the Clan in Los Angeles since the destruction of the second Temple (Another question: do these temple pre- or post-date the destruction of the Second Temple?).<br /> <br /> If nothing else, we must wonder if these are childer of Cavanaugh herself, of her rival Nicholas (Presuambly her own own Childe) or possibly even fresh blood imported into Los Angeles by the Setite Elders to make good Setite failures in the area (or some combination of the above): the exact answer will seriously affect the shape of local politics and intrigues across the Free States.<br /> <br /> <br /> (6) Finally, one has to wonder how aware the Sabbat, Camarilla and Setite assets in the Free States are of each other\u2019s operations - it occurs to me that, if they were aware of each other, they might well launch into a Shadow War less spectacular than the nightly action movie at the heart of the Free States, but more vicious.<br /> <br /> A Camarilla/Setite intrigue might be especially interesting (and damaging), since both could well be willing to sic the Anarchs on each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-05T17:09:46-08:00","id":1548997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites?p=1548991#post1548991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember correctly, Sir Ralph is one of the Brujah idealists - which might qualify him for the role of the mole who warned Dawn Cavanaugh away from the destruction of the second Temple, though for my money he might work better as a false lead in the Mole Hunt, given he doesn\u2019t seem especially close to MacNeil (Though as a Brujah with some Setite connections, he might be exactly the right Sire for our Mole).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sir Ralph is one of the four Brujah Idealists studying the Free States. He is unlikely to have been the mole though. First, something like that would have been explicitly mentioned in his character description. Second, he is not part of MacNeil's coterie. Third, although it is not stated when this group arrived in the Free States, since it contains Takuya Shiraiwa who was in Moscow until at least 1991, it implies the group had arrived only very recently (sometime during 1992-1994).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites?p=1548991#post1548991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think it would be quite important to establish who leads the Beverly Hills and Encino temples, because it seems highly likely that it is they and not Dawn Cavanaugh who have shaped the fortunes of the Clan in Los Angeles since the destruction of the second Temple (Another question: do these temple pre- or post-date the destruction of the Second Temple?).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b<br /> We're not given any dates as to when they were established, but it's implied they began sometime after Dawn's second temple was destroyed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites?p=1548991#post1548991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, one has to wonder how aware the Sabbat, Camarilla and Setite assets in the Free States are of each other\u2019s operations - it occurs to me that, if they were aware of each other, they might well launch into a Shadow War less spectacular than the nightly action movie at the heart of the Free States, but more vicious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Early edition material on the Setites imply that the Setites tend to be territorial and don't get along well with local temples often being rivals with one another unless a clear paramount power establishes personal control. So I'm inclined to run this as having these two temples and Dawn not get along with each other. Dawn views the Los Angeles area as properly being &quot;hers&quot;, and resents these upstarts sneaking in after she was forced to flee. In the chronicle, I will likely have the PCs learn about one of these other temples and allow them to take it out without realizing they were doing Dawn a favor (and likely being duped by her to do so). At the same time the PCs are discovering the presence of the Setites in LA, Dawn will be subduing these other temples under her control. It will make things more confusing and not as simple as the PCs will likely first think.<br /> <br /> In order to distinguish these two temples from each other and anything that Dawn does, I'll probably tie them into two different things. The Beverly Hills temple will control the local Scientology groups (or a fictionalized version of them) while the Encino branch will be associated with a local chapter of a fictionalized version of the real world Satanist group The Temple of Set (which split off from Anton Lavey's Church of Satan).<br /> <br /> Incidentally, Clanbook Setite 1e makes mention of a Death Valley Temple of Set, so I'll be adding that as factor as well although I'm not sure if it'll come into play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-05T17:13:41-08:00","id":1548998,"title":"","content":"The Setites in LABN are clearly the high priests of the Wyrm version of 1e/2e, not the genericization of the clan we would see beginning in Revised. So while the Setites are generally talked separately from other minions of the Wyrm, we may be able to make use of some of the Lupine content.<br /> <br /> In particular, there is a level two Pit underneath Griffith Park that contributes to LA being a \u201chaven of the weak and corrupt\u201d. There is a Black Spiral Dancer Hive there, and sometimes other Wyrm creatures make their way to the surface. I don\u2019t think it is a coincidence that Dawn\u2019s prior two temples were located not too far from there. (As are the other temples in Beverly Hills and Encino.) It\u2019s not mentioned that Dawn knows about this, but it\u2019s easy to justify Dawn discovering this and allying with the Dancers. While I wouldn\u2019t send a pack of BSDs against PCs, I could see myself using one BSD on some kind of mission that the PCs may come across.<br /> <br /> Rather than waiting for MacNeil to be destroyed (which may never happen in a chronicle), I think it\u2019s best for the chronicle if Dawn already sets in motion building a third temple. That provides a lot more things that the PCs can encounter.<br /> <br /> The first question is where should it be located? Dawn seems to prefer temples set in the Santa Monica Hills. The Malibu Hills and Hollywood Hills were both located there. Both were also relatively close to Griffith Park. Both places are also relatively affluent, but they aren\u2019t among the most expensive neighborhoods like the Platinum Triangle (Beverly Hills, Bel Air, and Holmby Hills). That may be because, per Setite Clanbook 1e, that the typical temple is located in a \u201cdesolate\u201d or unpopulated area in order to hide it from enemies. We can divide where Dawn might \u201centertain\u201d or corrupt versus where she conducts her religious rites and has her haven.<br /> <br /> If I want to go with the same pattern, I am thinking of putting her next temple in Los Feliz, a hillside neighborhood also in the Santa Monica Mountains just south of Griffith Park. That neighborhood also includes the site of the infamous Manson Family murders.<br /> <br /> I figure before Dawn herself returns, she\u2019ll send trusted minions to begin the process of finding fronts, surveying sites for the future temple, arranging construction materials, grooming herds, and so on. Some of that can become suspicious activity the PCs notice and can \u201cthwart\u201d without revealing Dawn.<br /> <br /> Then she\u2019ll arrive, perhaps as just another Kindred looking for freedom in LA. That will allow her to meet other Kindred and look for potential dupes to corrupt. She\u2019ll mainly keep to herself and only gradually expand the cult. After all, she wants to avoid attracting attention until she can figure out a way to destroy MacNeil and send the Free States in chaos. It\u2019ll provide an opportunity for PCs to run into her at some point. I\u2019ll just need to invent a persona for her like Helena did with \u201cPortia\u201d in CbN. Maybe something like Kirsten Bell\u2019s character Flora in Deadwood.<br /> <br /> Then I\u2019ll be ready for Setite style plots the PCs can run into before things eventually culminate in a hit upon MacNeil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T15:12:07-08:00","id":1549028,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, looking over your replies it strikes me that the Death Valley compound would make sense as mostly focused on recruitment &amp; indoctrination - with the Beverly Hills &amp; Encino temples staking a claim for primacy in LA, it\u2019s<br /> possible that those Setites who preferred to focus on building up the Clan, rather than tearing down their rivals (or at least valued their own skins too much to continue risking them in a town that had purged the Setites twice over).<br /> <br /> Incidentally, it\u2019s interesting to wonder if the Beverly Hills temple has extended any kind of feelers to the Toreador: assuming that their cult is legally-distinct version of Scientology, there\u2019s likely to be a strong celebrity element to mortal membership which could draw interest from the Hollywood Toreador (There\u2019s also some history of Clan Toreador doing business with the Serpents in LA and the Clan of the Rose is currently on the outs, so there may be enough overlap for the more ambitious players in both clans to put their heads together, knowingly or unknowingly).<br /> <br /> <br /> On a wider scale, it\u2019s interesting to wonder if the two temples in Los Angeles represent survivors of the two camps which disputed the rule of the second LA temple back in the early Seventies - it\u2019s possible that the only thing which might unite them is the prospect of Dawn Cavanaugh seeking to reassert herself after decades of absence.<br /> <br /> Also, one wonders if Cavanaugh would seek recruits from any of the three California temples or if she\u2019d prefer to rely on a small cabal of recruits drawn from her time in Chicago (Given her Nature as a Conspirator, I suspect she prefers to work with small groups of like-minded individuals rather than making any kind of grass-roots appeal).<br /> <br /> Actually, there\u2019s also the question of whether she left any kind of establishment in San Francisco or moved all her assets in that city into Los Angeles in order to construct the second Temple.<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, for my own amusement I took your suggestion of a cult that was absolutely not Scientology, but could pass for Scientology in a dark alley in the dead of night and tried to puzzle out some names for such a thing - at this point I have Xenoism, Techgnosticism, Psientology, Quantum Divinity and Circuitology.<br /> <br /> Please feel free to pick any of the above or leave them one &amp; all.\ud83d\ude42","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T18:08:13-08:00","id":1549039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites?p=1549028#post1549028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">looking over your replies it strikes me that the Death Valley compound would make sense as mostly focused on recruitment &amp; indoctrination - with the Beverly Hills &amp; Encino temples staking a claim for primacy in LA, it\u2019s<br /> possible that those Setites who preferred to focus on building up the Clan, rather than tearing down their rivals (or at least valued their own skins too much to continue risking them in a town that had purged the Setites twice over).</div> </div> </div> </div>After posting that, I reread that section in Clanbook Setite. It turns out Death Valley isn't just &quot;a&quot; temple of Set, but one of the major temples of Set with a &quot;High Priest&quot;, one of the elder Setites who are in communion with the Antedeluvian in dreams who not only know the plans for the Jyhad, but how Set intends to rule the world post-Gehenna.<br /> <br /> <i>In all these temples can be found the wailing, rotting High Priests of Typhon, the transcendent individuals who have pursued the Path of Typhon to its foulest limits. These creatures are believed by many to be the eyes and mouths of sleeping Set, and their ghastly ululations and insane pronouncements are eagerly attended by the faithful, and examined for prophecies and omens. It is these high-priests of corruption who lead the Path of Typhon on towards its insane goal.</i><br /> <br /> So it is clearly the elder temple in the area.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites?p=1549028#post1549028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a wider scale, it\u2019s interesting to wonder if the two temples in Los Angeles represent survivors of the two camps which disputed the rule of the second LA temple back in the early Seventies - it\u2019s possible that the only thing which might unite them is the prospect of Dawn Cavanaugh seeking to reassert herself after decades of absence.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's plausible that any survivors might have remained behind and established their own temples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites?p=1549028#post1549028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, one wonders if Cavanaugh would seek recruits from any of the three California temples or if she\u2019d prefer to rely on a small cabal of recruits drawn from her time in Chicago (Given her Nature as a Conspirator, I suspect she prefers to work with small groups of like-minded individuals rather than making any kind of grass-roots appeal).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Dawn clearly saw her time in Chicago as a &quot;wait until I'm ready&quot; period. As such, she would not have wanted to do anything that would either set the powers in that city against her, or would tie her down into that city. Not only would siring create problems for her with the Prince (Lodin had forbid siring, and anyone wanting to do so went to Gary and Prince Modius instead), it's not certain any childe sired in Chicago would want to leave.<br /> <br /> If she had childer in Los Angeles who survived when she fled, she may have stayed in contact with them though and arranged for them to meet her when she returns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites?p=1549028#post1549028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, for my own amusement I took your suggestion of a cult that was absolutely not Scientology, but could pass for Scientology in a dark alley in the dead of night and tried to puzzle out some names for such a thing - at this point I have Xenoism, Techgnosticism, Psientology, Quantum Divinity and Circuitology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowing my own player base, I'd be going with MindHead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jYQZ-RmBHpk\" data-code=\"jYQZ-RmBHpk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/jYQZ-RmBHpk/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-07T04:50:30-08:00","id":1549045,"title":"","content":"\u201cYou are very wise for one who has lived not even a single lifetime\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> On a less serious note, this whole set-up becomes even more hilarious if people keep looking at a cult leader with the face of Terence Stamp (With an Evil Goatee, obviously, because this is The World of Darkness and I have a shameless sense of whimsy) and keep asking themselves \u201cHe\u2019s got to be the Boss Vampire, right? You can\u2019t have Terence Stamp in a vampire game and <i>not</i> make him a Boss Vampire, right? There are <i>rules</i>.\u201d<br /> <br /> Bonus points if the character played by Mr Terence Stamp is <i>not</i> actually a vampire, but is being used as a very helpful decoy by a much less impressive-looking figure (Think Mr Philip Seymour Hoffman with fangs?).<br /> <br /> <br /> (1) Indeed the Death Valley compound is not only a temple but a veritable Setite oracle - no wonder it\u2019s elder hasn\u2019t taken the other California temples in hand, if they\u2019re busy gibberish in the throes of Lovecraftian visions (and their most important subordinates are presumably too busy making sure nobody takes advantage of this distraction to stick their oar in).<br /> <br /> \u2026.<br /> <br /> Now we must ask ourselves when this Great Big Important Setite established themselves in California (Being presumably older than the United States and very possibly older than the post-Columbian Interchange): presumably they arrived after Dawn Cavanaugh, whilst the latter was in good odour with Don Sebastian (Though how much Cavanaugh or any of the other local Setites know about the Death Valley temple is an interesting question).<br /> <br /> Incidentally, learning of this \u2018Elder temple\u2019 makes me wonder if the very youthful Cavanaugh is meant as much as a distraction from the Death Valley Elder as she is a key player in her own right \u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> (2) I do think that making the two temples descendants of the two factions - very possibly peopled by Setites mostly descended from Dawn Cavanaugh herself and her own brood - lends an interesting angle to the LA Followers of Set (Making it as much a family quarrel as a schism).<br /> <br /> Incidentally, one must wonder whether it was purely personal ambition that drove the feud between Cavanaugh &amp; Nicholas or if there was some element of ideological differences that fuelled this very damaging split (One of them being, perhaps, more willing to borrow from Anarch philosophy or less willing to risk association with Lupines of any stripe).<br /> <br /> <br /> (3) I think the question is less \u201cDid Dawn Cavanaugh have childer in Los Angeles?\u201d and more \u201cHow large a brood did she produce and how do the survivors - and their descendants - feel about their Sire?\u201d<br /> <br /> After all, Cavanaugh was at the head of Setite efforts in LA for roughly a quarter century before the Second Anarch Revolt and in good odour with the Prince - plenty of time for her to establish a brood - and it\u2019s hard to imagine the Anarchs keeping an especially close eye on Setite numbers if they didn\u2019t even notice the second Temple until it was pointed out to them (and have yet to rumble the Beverly Hills &amp; Encino temples).<br /> <br /> The real question is whether the Setites of the Death Valley temple (Presumably older than Cavanaugh and of a lower generation) allow any of their descendants to risk themselves (and the temple) by recruiting in the Big City.<br /> <br /> So far as I can see, they\u2019re the only known alternative to Dawn Cavanaugh in terms of Embracing Setites in the Free States (Especially given that Followers of Set tend to prefer to choose new Setites from within their mortal cults).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-07T05:15:55-08:00","id":1549046,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Djoser_Jones\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Djoser_Jones</a><br /> <br /> By the way, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, I stumbled onto this character whilst trying to find a list of Followers of Set tend - trying to puzzle out if there were any other plausible candidate for Cavanaugh\u2019s sire than Abu Ruhadze - and can only say that he fits Los Angeles perfectly.<br /> <br /> His generation (11th) is too low for him to be a descendant of Dawn Cavanaugh (8th) herself - unless her brood multiplied at alarming speed, which seems unlikely - but his having been acquired as a ghoul circa AD 1924 and Embraced in 1934 makes perfect sense within the context of the first Temple\u2019s timeline and the fact he goes his separate way from his Sire in 1944 works even more perfectly if one assumes the \u2018big city\u2019 they ran off to not long after the Reverend\u2019s embrace was Los Angeles.<br /> <br /> Heck, one can even explain plausibly explain Sisocharis\u2019 spending such a lengthy period in small town California as their playing some role in establishing (or at least securing) the site of the Death Valley temple, which I suspect to have been established at this time.<br /> <br /> Whether Sisocharis was a direct subordinate of Dawn Cavanaugh is, of course, an interesting question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-07T17:18:39-08:00","id":1549062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites?p=1549045#post1549045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bonus points if the character played by Mr Terence Stamp is <i>not</i> actually a vampire, but is being used as a very helpful decoy by a much less impressive-looking figure (Think Mr Philip Seymour Hoffman with fangs?).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a bad idea to use someone like Terence Stamp in the above as the mortal face of Scientology/MindHead, and then someone like Hoffman as the behind the scene Setite who eventually reveals at some point the truth, except it being about Set and not Xenu. Stamp doesn't even have to be a ghoul, but a mortal agent (willing or not) who sends certain people to vampire Hoffman that Hoffman's identified as being particularly interesting to him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Iw54-yDc6Jg\" data-code=\"Iw54-yDc6Jg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Iw54-yDc6Jg/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I wonder if it'd a good distinction having the Beverly Hills temple be more concerned about infiltrating mortal society, and having the Encino temple more willing to deal with the supernatural. The real life &quot;Satanic&quot; Temple of Set is heavily involved in thelema style magick, and combined with the portrayal of Setite blood sorcery, perhaps that temple could &quot;corrupt&quot; Kindred by the targeted selection of certain anarchs to learn some form of &quot;anarch thaumaturgy&quot;.<br /> <br /> The role of blood magic among the anarchs is something I want to explore in the setting as a whole. The absence of the Tremere and Giovanni means the Free States are somewhat magic starved, but also allows for an independent flourishing of its study. The setting as a whole became much more open to the idea of non-Tremere knowing blood sorcery than when LABN was written. So much like the Chicago Tremere in CBN1e were teaching Gordon Keaton some Thaumaturgy in exchange for being their catspaw, and I could do the same here. I already had in mind some coterie having enough Movement of Mind to fly like the vampires in The Lost Boys, and perhaps they (or at least their leader) are tied in with this Setite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites?p=1549045#post1549045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now we must ask ourselves when this Great Big Important Setite established themselves in California (Being presumably older than the United States and very possibly older than the post-Columbian Interchange): presumably they arrived after Dawn Cavanaugh, whilst the latter was in good odour with Don Sebastian (Though how much Cavanaugh or any of the other local Setites know about the Death Valley temple is an interesting question).<br /> <br /> Incidentally, learning of this \u2018Elder temple\u2019 makes me wonder if the very youthful Cavanaugh is meant as much as a distraction from the Death Valley Elder as she is a key player in her own right \u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously there is no canonical answer, and it's highly likely the author of Clanbook Setite did not bother to think about LABN when he wrote down that bit about a Death Valley temple and it being home to a High Priest. However, I imagine it probably was created after Dawn's arrival in Los Angeles and her identification of that city as a great potential source of corruption. She probably was involved in helping arrange matters so the Death Valley temple could be built, likely during the rule of Don Sebastian.<br /> <br /> I think Setite temples are independent and not in any strict hierarchy like the Tremere Pyramid. But there is obviously some sort or hierarchy in the sense that certain temples are considered more senior and important. CBS1e only mentions five high temples (London, Rome, New York, New Orleans, Death Valley), but I imagine there are more unmentioned outside of Europe and North America. However, I am going to go that within North America at least, those three high temples do oversee in some capacity a division of the continent. NYC the Eastern Seaboard and Midwest, New Orleans the South, and Death Valley the West Coast, Southwest, the Rockies, and Mexico. Since the Setites have a wide ranging variety of foes and interests (not just vampires), I imagine the Death Valley temple has a lot more on its plate than just LA. Still, if Dawn wants to unleash Amam the Devourer to eat Jeremy MacNeil, she likely needs permission and authorization from whatever is at the Death Valley temple of Set.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites?p=1549045#post1549045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all, Cavanaugh was at the head of Setite efforts in LA for roughly a quarter century before the Second Anarch Revolt and in good odour with the Prince - plenty of time for her to establish a brood - and it\u2019s hard to imagine the Anarchs keeping an especially close eye on Setite numbers if they didn\u2019t even notice the second Temple until it was pointed out to them (and have yet to rumble the Beverly Hills &amp; Encino temples).</div> </div> </div> </div>Are all the Setite vampires secret in the sense they are completely unknown to the Kindred in LA? If they were just corrupting mortals they could be, but if they are trying to corrupt Kindred I would think they must be known. And if they are known, what clans do they disguise themselves as? Considering that the mere identification of a temple was enough for MacNeil to attack and wipe it out, I imagine the Setites must disguise themselves here. Since the Toreador are somewhat frowned upon, I think they probably pose as particularly Presence using Brujah and hope for the best.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-07T17:51:56-08:00","id":1549064,"title":"","content":"(1) Another useful point of distinction between the two temples would likely be the question would be whether they favour \u2018Top down\u2019 or \u2018Grass roots\u2019 methods of corruption - are they aiming to convert an elite and then shake down the rest of the social pyramid or are they looking to set the wider community afire?<br /> <br /> <br /> (2) Given your mention of the Setites using blood magic as a possible stock in trade when dealing with local Anarchs, you might consider having at least some of them present as Tremere <i>antitribu</i> (Possibly even runaways from the Sabbat, though I\u2019m not sure how open the Free States would be to that sort of crowd).<br /> <br /> Presenting at Caitiff might also be possible, albeit more high-risk: I vaguely recall that some Setite disciplines conjure up ophidian features, so Kindred experiencing this affliction could try passing themselves off as City Gangrel (or as Gangrel taking a tour of a city).<br /> <br /> Heck, if they get desperate enough they might even pretend to be Giovanni!<br /> <br /> <br /> (3) My guess is that High Temples are less an institution and more of a phenomenon - they accumulate around an elder who has gone so much closer to Set than almost any other that they inspire a following willing to watch over them (and listen in on their speaking in tongues) for as long as the Elders are pleased to commune with their terrible deity, not to mention follow them whenever they are moved to \u2018up sticks\u2019 and also rebuild wherever they are pleased to seat themselves.<br /> <br /> So while it\u2019s a near-certainty that High Temples have existed in locations other than those mentioned above, I tend to imagine that their numbers have always been limited and their location only rarely pre-planned.<br /> <br /> The fact that three of the high temples have established themselves on United States soil should therefore quite definitely be regarded as a very rare phenomenon indeed - and one as yet inexplicable to wholly rational minds.<br /> <br /> <br /> (4) I definitely agree that the Death Valley temple has much more to consider than LA alone, though I tend to imagine it leveraging soft power rather than set-in-stone authority (With the local elder being treated as an Oracle, with their supporters exercising influence by interpreting their strange gift of tongues in almost exactly the same way the priesthood at Ancient Delphi shared &amp; disseminated the Pythian oracles - and the fact that the founding myth of Delphi involved the destruction of dragon with the name of a great serpent by a solar deity suggests some interesting things in a World of Darkness context.<br /> <br /> Whether these followers are reading more into this gift of tongues than is there to be heard (and how much conscious control over this babbling the elders have) probably varies with the high temple in question.<br /> <br /> <br /> (5) I suspect that at the very least Followers of Set in LA prefer to be known as vampires, but not as Setites - and that at least one of the temples would advocate extreme secrecy whilst the other calls for more misdirection than evasion.<br /> <br /> Honestly, there are quite a few questions still to be answered and one looks forward to seeing more of your efforts to answer them and flesh out the ranks of Los Angeles Setites (Out of curiosity, might I please ask if you thought my identification of Djoser Jones as a Setite likely to have strong LA connections at all plausible?).<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, Best Wishes and have a very lovely weekend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-10T14:55:28-07:00","id":1549136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites?p=1549064#post1549064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another useful point of distinction between the two temples would likely be the question would be whether they favour \u2018Top down\u2019 or \u2018Grass roots\u2019 methods of corruption - are they aiming to convert an elite and then shake down the rest of the social pyramid or are they looking to set the wider community afire?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't think about things that way, but it is a convenient distinction about approaches. Given Dawn's preference for &quot;corrupting&quot; Kindred over mortals, and the temples always being located in affluent areas, it seems the local Setites are pursuing a top down approach overall. If I ever decide to add yet another temple, I might go a different route.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites?p=1549064#post1549064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given your mention of the Setites using blood magic as a possible stock in trade when dealing with local Anarchs, you might consider having at least some of them present as Tremere <i>antitribu</i> (Possibly even runaways from the Sabbat, though I\u2019m not sure how open the Free States would be to that sort of crowd).</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the hostility of the Free States to the Sabbat, I think even trying to pursue a &quot;Sabbat, but we're defectors&quot; would be even more hazardous than just admitting their Setites.<br /> <br /> There is some early edition references to Anarch Thaumaturgy. The Anarch Cookbook references alchemy, anarch rituals, curses, and possibly even countermagickal &quot;anti-rituals&quot; (including this Anarch Cookbook info in the chronicle is one of my goals). In my chronicles, I got tired of having a Tremere monopoly on blood magic when it seemed everyone else outside the Camarilla knew some paths. So I created a list of pre-Tremere Paths that were not exclusive to the Tremere, and even a secret society of blood sorcerers within the Camarilla that preserved knowledge of them so the Tremere did not have a monopoly on magic. So having some anarchs know some arcane secrets is not hard to justify in my chronicles. If anything, these &quot;facts&quot; would make the Free States the safest place to teach and learn this blood magic among the anarchs. Having one or two Setite infiltrators here won't be too hard as there will be various low level &quot;amateur&quot; magician practitioners among the anarchs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites?p=1549064#post1549064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, if they get desperate enough they might even pretend to be Giovanni!</div> </div> </div> </div>The Free States don't seem to be keen on the Giovanni either. The possible angle that the Giovanni might be useful to anarchs against the local Prince doesn't really work in the Free States themselves. There are no Giovanni NPCs listed in the book, and the only mention of the clan is that the Giovanni sees the instability cause by the anarchs as bad for business. They are trying to prevent anarchs from disrupting or taking over their local strongpoint of Las Vegas which means the closest Giovanni are de facto helping the Camarilla. Furthermore, I think the overall philosophy of the anarchs doesn't match well with a clan being ruled outright by a thousand year old elder of the third generation.<br /> <br /> So while a Giovanni guise might prove better than admitting you're a Setite, it's probably best you just stick with the typical clans.<br /> <br /> I might place a single Giovanni spy in Los Angeles, but her purpose will be solely intelligence gathering and will avoid the most obvious Giovanni interests so that she does not attract attention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites?p=1549064#post1549064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Out of curiosity, might I please ask if you thought my identification of Djoser Jones as a Setite likely to have strong LA connections at all plausible?).</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't be using that character, or a similar one, for my own chronicle as it doesn't fit what I'll be doing with the clan in this setting. There is nothing inherently wrong with a Setite concept based on some fraudulent revivalist preacher, but it's just not something I associate with southern California. I'm sure such people can be found there as anywhere else, but it doesn't seem as natural to that locale as opposed to the Deep South for example.<br /> <br /> This particular write up does bear the marks of things I did not like about the Revised era depiction. It really wants to ditch the Robert E Howard view of &quot;Set&quot; for something else, but is trapped by continuity and so it tries to do it in a very contrived way. Why does he think Set &quot;forgives&quot; when there is absolutely nothing about that religion that involves forgiveness in any way? Permissiveness is not the same as forgiveness. Why does he still cling to the idea as Set as a god when he is disenchanted enough to abandon &quot;vice-mongering&quot; which is core to the religion? As written, I can't imagine why the Setites wouldn't destroy him and embrace someone better fitted.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, if he's intended as a Jim Jones type character (which can fit in a California setting because Jones, of course, made his mark in radical left circles in San Francisco), he doesn't really work. Jim Jones was an atheist Communist who became a reverend because he thought it was a good way to fool gullible people into becoming Marxists. Moving from the conservative Midwest to left wing San Francisco allowed him to find various allies to help him. Such a character too might be &quot;corrupted&quot; by the Setites and switch allegiances, but this character as written is far more of someone who was initially sincere in his faith, but far too weak in morals and character. Nothing like the ruthless political operative, sacrilegious, and egomaniacal cult leader he is supposedly based on.<br /> <br /> If I was going to include such a character concept for this chronicle, I'd write up an entirely new character than the one presented on that wikipage. If someone else can use the character as is in their own version of the Free States, good for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-11T10:36:08-07:00","id":1549156,"title":"","content":"In all fairness, given the Followers of Set are so explicitly grounded in religion it seems logical that more than a few of them have (whether through selfish cynicism or genuine conviction) redefined Set in exactly the fashion best suited to serve their own needs.<br /> <br /> Heck, given their explicit commitment to undermining any given Status Quo (and tendency to treat internecine rivalries as the order of the day) it would be more astonishing if the Followers of Set were not prone to throw up as many heresies, schisms, hypocrisies and self-serving charlatans as Christianity.<br /> <br /> Whether these hypocrites and charlatans last long enough to seriously affect the shape of the Clan is, of course, an interesting question.<br /> <br /> <br /> DIGRESSION: Incidentally, one of my more inspiring discoveries on the White Wolf Wiki was the revelation that - in AD 1520 - a Setite named Lucretia (6th Generation) had Embraced Danny Larkhill and Mark Sandhurst, who would go on to become antitribu and Camarilla archons.<br /> <br /> Since my original search had been for \u2018Lucretia\u2019 (Seeking to get a better understanding of who the stereotypical Snake Priestess destroyed in Modern London by the PC &amp; his coterie in VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE - REDEMPTION might have been), being handed the perfect excuse to make her a contemporary of Lucrezia Borgia whose various escapades inspired the \u2018Black Legend\u2019 associated with that relatively blameless historic individual (Not least through her own muck-slinging), all of which earned her Embrace by the Followers of Set (After which point she promptly applied the classic Borgia \u201cGod has given us the Papacy, let us enjoy it!\u201d mixture of piety, hypocrisy, lethality and \u2018merriment\u2019 to her career, growing into the living cliche of a Setite and a surprisingly-heavy hitter*).<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>*If nothing else through Generation, showmanship, audacity and completely shamelessness realpolitik, very much in the style of Renaissance prince - secular or sacred.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Moving on, your suggestion that the Giovannia are rare and fairly discrete in the Free States makes me wonder which of the Clans would be most likely to monopolise - or seek to monopolise - local bastions of Organised Crime (Beyond the street gangs focused upon in LOS ANGELES BY NIGHT).<br /> <br /> The Ventrue, perhaps? Ventrue with aspirations towards their traditional preeminence over the levers of civic &amp; commercial power would seem to be mistrusted by the Anarchs (and it\u2019s interesting to wonder if Don Sebastian was also reluctant to let the Clan of Kings get too close to the pillars of the Establishment in his city, given the character\u2019s apparent love of Control) so pursuing less legitimate business might be a Free State Ventrue\u2019s best bet for getting some power and authority without starting to look TOO much like \u2018The Man\u2019.<br /> <br /> I may have noted this before, but I really like the idea of the Free States as a place where Kindred can (and are sometimes positively obliged to) spend their nights in a way that upends the classic expectations of their Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-11T17:48:25-07:00","id":1549173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites?p=1549156#post1549156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all fairness, given the Followers of Set are so explicitly grounded in religion it seems logical that more than a few of them have (whether through selfish cynicism or genuine conviction) redefined Set in exactly the fashion best suited to serve their own needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see the Setites as less of a &quot;religion&quot; than a cult. Cults don't tolerate independent thinkers or heretics. The purpose of the cult is to control their members on behalf of their leader. If someone diverges too much, they get destroyed. Of course, not all of them get flamed. The Serpents of the Light managed to survive by defecting to the Sabbat, and I'm sure there were many previous heretics who managed to survive for a little while and some who remain surviving still. But those are outliers. (Of course, even cults have power struggles, but usually this is about power, money, and influence, not independent theologies.)<br /> <br /> One major issue that I have always had with the sourcebooks on the Followers of Set, is that the writers too often want them to be portrayed just like any other clan, and this problem has gotten worse with every new edition. In my chronicles, Setites almost always exclusively embrace only from the inner circles of the Setite cult and thus deal with vampires whose mortals selves have already been effectively brainwashed. Now like with all things, there are of course exceptions. Sometimes Setites do decide spontaneously to embrace someone outside the cult, or misjudge how effectively brainwashed a member is. That's fine. But these exceptions are a small minority.<br /> <br /> I know many people prefer the newer depiction of the Setites than the older ones, but I like my snake cults.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites?p=1549156#post1549156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moving on, your suggestion that the Giovannia are rare and fairly discrete in the Free States makes me wonder which of the Clans would be most likely to monopolise - or seek to monopolise - local bastions of Organised Crime (Beyond the street gangs focused upon in LOS ANGELES BY NIGHT).</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine organized crime in LA is not monopolized by Kindred from any specific clan. The Los Angeles crime family is much weaker compared to other Mafia families, and have been in decline since the 1950s. So real life suggests there isn't one Kindred &quot;controlling&quot; the family. There are probably several different Kindred pulling strings which makes the family divided and less effective than their rivals.<br /> <br /> I do intend to have some call outs to famous depictions of LA crime families particularly those elements highlighted by the books of James Ellroy, and especially the movie version of LA Confidential.<br /> <br /> In my chronicle, I'll be having David Geduld's &quot;gang&quot; having some significant influence, particularly in regards to the ports and smuggling. The other Kindred involved will reside in the Barony of Angels, but not necessarily be members of the MacNeil Boys. Smiling Jack has influence in a major criminal motorcycle gang. Simply because the Brujah make up 50% of the Kindred in the Free States, the Kindred of that clan probably make up most of the Kindred with influence in organized crime. Geduld's line of Ventrue has some. Some Caitiff do as well. The other clans not so much. I intend for the Setites to have influence in some &quot;adjacent&quot; industries like porn studios and the like, but not in the crime family itself.<br /> <br /> In terms of Giovanni and organized crime, I have my own fictional version of New York's Five Families pulled from other fictional settings (notably the Godfather) and one of these is the Putanesca Crime Family which the Giovanni control through that family. The clan tends to be &quot;locked out&quot; of any other crime family, but control of the Putanesca still gives them a lot of reach in my chronicles.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-12T13:26:50-07:00","id":1549201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know many people prefer the newer depiction of the Setites than the older ones, but I like my snake cults. </div> </div> </div> They\u2019re always easiest to love from the safe distance of a whole dimensional continuum away.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On a more serious note, I\u2019m happy to incorporate both (Since the World of Darkness is a place with plenty of room for Evil Snake Cults and equally-Evil cults with slightly more diverse branding).<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, it might amuse you to know that I had already started to think of LA\u2019s least favourite resident Ventrue of the early 1990s (Competition with Baron Fortier was <i>fierce</i>) and his coterie as \u2018Task Force Ex\u2019 - as in \u2018Ex-Camarilla\u2019 and \u2018Suicide Squad\u2019 - but your mention of LA CONFIDENTIAL now gives me an excuse to think of this as an additional homage to Ed Exley and his police colleagues\u2019 warm interpersonal relationships.<br /> <br /> Yes, that last bit <i>was</i> sarcasm: I\u2019m British, it\u2019s the national sport.<br /> <br /> <br /> On a more serious note, it occurred to me at one point that Geduld and his ex-Camarilla coterie could well serve as Jeremy MacNeil\u2019s equivalent to the WHITE HOUSE PLUMBERS (I.E. Deniable assets who do the sort of discrete work the Camarilla specialises in, but which a good Anarch simply cannot afford to countenance \u2026 that\u2019s Task Force Ex\u2019s story, at least).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}